Z||000000||chris6878||02-12-2001||03:16 AM||||Hi everyone,<P>Been a while since my last post... but here goes..<P>My 85 gt was running perfect, then one night i was out with my g/f and it starts backfiring when I press the gas 1/2 the way or more. But the car made it home, a little slower than usual..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">         but anyway.. the next day i went out to start her, she started and immediately quit when pressing the gas. Now all it will do is attempt to start when the motor turns, it will hit and almost start when i press the gas pedal to the floor, but never starts, just almost starts.    it has new dis shaft (ign module, pickup coil included)   , dist cap, rotor, new plugs and wires and gas filter.         any ideals on the problem..                       I am getting gas to the fuel rail...   i was thinknig maybe i might have got some bad gas, fuel pump or my ignition coil is going south...  <P>any suggestions would be greatly appreciated..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>thanks in advance,<BR>chris||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||02-12-2001||07:27 AM||||Sounds like either a tach filter or ignition module.<P>Unplug the tach filter and see if it runs ok.  If it does, you've found the problem.  Rodney Dickman sells replacements.||||reg||1
